1
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:08,120
- Hey. - Hi.

2
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,460
Pheebs, what's wrong?

3
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:11,550
I'm just so exhausted from dragging around

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,320
this huge engagement ring.

5
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:14,850
Oh, my God.

6
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:16,210
Congratulations.

7
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:17,990
So did he get on one knee?

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,700
Did he have a speech prepared?

9
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:21,350
Oh, did he cry?

10
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:26,170
Yeah, big surprise, I like proposals.

11
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,390
Well, it was really sweet,

12
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:31,630
and, like, the most romantic thing ever.

13
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:33,380
Here's to Phoebe,

14
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:35,220
who's found the greatest guy in the world.

15
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:36,430
To Phoebe and--

16
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,170
I want to say "Mike"?

17
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:40,660
To Phoebe and Mike.

18
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:42,910
Thank you.

19
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,640
Oh, and I have something for you.

20
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,650
It's my little black book.

21
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,600
It's got the numbers of all the guys I've dated.

22
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,990
Oh, Phoebe, that's nice,

23
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:53,300
but you know what? I think I'm okay.

24
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,180
Why don't you just give it

25
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:55,590
to one of your other single girlfriends.

26
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,470
I would, but you're the last one.

27
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:00,900
Give me the book!

28
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:04,700
"Pablo Diaz.

29
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:06,530
Brady Smith.

30
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:09,460
Guy in Van"?

31
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:11,060
Oh, my first love.

32
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,630
What is the red X next to

33
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:16,170
Bob Gremore's name mean?

34
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:17,150
Dead.

35
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:22,150
Oh, it's okay. No, he was old. Yeah.

36
00:01:22,710 --> 00:01:23,760
And he lived a full life.

37
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:26,170
He was in the first wave at Omaha Beach.

38
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:29,610
oh, I'm sorry. I should've given you guys my black book

39
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,840
when I got married.

40
00:01:30,890 --> 00:01:32,010
Although, it wasn't so much a book

41
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:33,400
as a napkin.

42
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:37,020
With Janice's phone number on it.

43
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:41,090
Phoebe, isn't Jethro Tull a band?

44
00:01:45,390 --> 00:01:46,850
Oh, yes, they are.

45
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,850
Friends S10E06 The One With Ross's Grant

46
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:29,320
Hey, honey.

47
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:31,550
Hey, sweetie.

48
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,070
- Is Monica not here? - No.

49
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,610
Then I'll tell you.

50
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:38,390
My agency was bidding for a big account, and they got it.

51
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,090
It's my first national commercial.

52
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:40,910
Cool.

53
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:41,940
And I don't want to brag,

54
00:02:41,990 --> 00:02:43,730
but a lot of the ideas were mine.

55
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:45,440
Hell, you weren't there.

56
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:46,830
All the ideas were mine.

57
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,830
That's great.

58
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,120
Hey, can you cast me in it?

59
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:54,360
I really don't think you're right for the part.

60
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,930
What do you mean? I can do anything.

61
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:57,490
I'm a chameleon.

62
00:02:59,490 --> 00:03:00,780
I'm old.

63
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,310
I'm tired.

64
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,310
Oh, I am hot. I'm cold.

65
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,610
Come on, what can't I do?

66
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:12,930
First of all, bravo.

67
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,930
But I don't think you're right for this.

68
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:18,200
The part's a stuffy college professor.

69
00:03:18,250 --> 00:03:19,670
I can do that.

70
00:03:19,890 --> 00:03:22,160
Hello, I'm your professor.

71
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,570
When I'm not busy thinking of important things,

72
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:26,830
or professing...

73
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:30,250
...l like to use-- What's the product?

74
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:33,960
Software that facilitates inter-business networking e-solutions.

75
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:40,440
I'm cold.

76
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:44,810
- Hey. - Hey.

77
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:45,940
Guess who's a finalist

78
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:48,010
for a huge research grant?

79
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:49,000
I'll give you a hint.

80
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:50,170
He's looking right at you.

81
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,160
Well, unless it's the creepy guy

82
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:54,750
with his hand up his kilt...

83
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,650
...I'm gonna say, "Congratulations."

84
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,820
I'm so excited.

85
00:03:58,870 --> 00:04:02,190
Apparently, I beat out hundreds of other applicants...

86
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:05,020
...including five guys I went to graduate school with.

87
00:04:05,070 --> 00:04:07,830
Not that I'm keeping score, or anything. Five.

88
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,700
- Wow, that's great. - Yeah.

89
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:11,790
So tell me about the grant.

90
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,850
Well, okay, it's for $25,000.

91
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:15,030
And if I get it,

92
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:17,500
I'll be able to complete my field research.

93
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:19,550
And there will be an article about me

94
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,500
in the Paleontology Review.

95
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:23,730
It'll be the first time my name is in there...

96
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:26,420
...without people raising serious questions about my work.

97
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:30,170
Are you talking about the Dewer Grant?

98
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,180
Yeah. Why?

99
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:33,520
Benjamin Hobart is administering that grant.

100
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:35,720
- Your ex-boyfriend? - Yeah.

101
00:04:35,770 --> 00:04:38,040
So your ex-boyfriend is gonna determine

102
00:04:38,090 --> 00:04:40,360
if your new boyfriend gets this grant?

103
00:04:40,410 --> 00:04:42,430
Wow, your new boyfriend is screwed.

104
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:46,040
No. No, we ended on great terms.

105
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:46,800
I mean if anything,

106
00:04:46,850 --> 00:04:48,040
I think this could help you. You know what?

107
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:50,400
Why don't we all go out to dinner,

108
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:51,670
and I can introduce you.

109
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:53,320
If you think it'd help.

110
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:55,070
Yeah, absolutely. I'll call him.

111
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,990
Now, is there anything I could do to butter him up?

112
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,750
Anything he really likes?

113
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:03,240
He does have a pretty serious latex fetish.

114
00:05:03,290 --> 00:05:04,840
We'll see how dinner goes.

115
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:12,120
- Hey. - Hey, you want to go see a movie?

116
00:05:12,910 --> 00:05:15,270
I told you I had to spend all day clearing out stuff

117
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,520
so Mike could move in.

118
00:05:16,570 --> 00:05:18,140
- Oh, right. - Yeah.

119
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,250
Now that I'm here,

120
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,650
I might as well help with the cleaning and organizing.

121
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:25,110
I just happen to have my label maker.

122
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:29,400
Oh, it's so hard to get rid of stuff.

123
00:05:29,450 --> 00:05:31,410
Did you and Chandler make compromises

124
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:32,870
when you moved in together?

125
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,410
Chandler did.

126
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,000
What does he want you to give up?

127
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:38,160
A bunch of stuff.

128
00:05:38,210 --> 00:05:39,550
And the worst one,

129
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,500
he wants me to get rid of Gladys.

130
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:43,200
Who's Gladys?

131
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,220
What a tragic loss.

132
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:52,410
Yeah, I really hate to give her up.

133
00:05:52,730 --> 00:05:54,850
Oh, I know. Oh, you should take her.

134
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:00,040
I don't know.

135
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,650
What, you don't like her?

136
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:06,150
Of course I do. What's not to like?

137
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:08,680
I'd take her in a minute.

138
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,880
But I think that you're giving up too easy.

139
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:14,190
Honey, I think that you need to fight for her.

140
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:17,550
- Really, you think? - Absolutely.

141
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,820
You say to him,

142
00:06:18,870 --> 00:06:20,840
"I'm sorry, Mike, I can't live without her.

143
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:22,760
She means too much to me."

144
00:06:23,510 --> 00:06:26,340
Okay, I'll fight for her. Okay.

145
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,360
Oh, wait. I just realized, if I do that,

146
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:30,630
that means you don't get her.

147
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,740
Damn it, I did not think this through.

148
00:06:36,790 --> 00:06:38,750
- Hey, guys. - Hey.

149
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:40,650
Oh, any word on casting yet?

150
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,820
I told you, you're not right for the part.

151
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:44,030
What do you mean?

152
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,760
Rach, don't I seem like a professor

153
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:47,970
you'd buy some kind of e-crap from?

154
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:50,040
I'm sorry,

155
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:52,300
this sounds like something I'm never gonna be interested in.

156
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:55,220
Look, come on, please?

157
00:06:55,270 --> 00:06:58,100
It's not like I'm asking you for some crazy favor.

158
00:06:58,260 --> 00:06:59,320
This is what I do for a living.

159
00:06:59,370 --> 00:07:01,130
I am a professional actor.

160
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,260
Man, I'm two hours late for work.

161
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,450
Here's a copy of my reel.

162
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,330
It's got all the commercials that I've been in.

163
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:10,190
- Joe-- - Just watch it.

164
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,070
If you don't like it,

165
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,090
don't pass it on to your bosses.

166
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:15,380
- Fine. - Thank you.

167
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:22,420
- Work, Joe. - Damn it.

168
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:27,370
What am I gonna do now?

169
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:28,690
Just pass the tape along.

170
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,470
He's not right for the part.

171
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,430
If I suggest him,

172
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,180
my bosses will think I'm an idiot.

173
00:07:33,230 --> 00:07:35,410
And that's something they should learn on their own.

174
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:38,420
Just tell Joey that you watched the tape...

175
00:07:38,470 --> 00:07:40,590
...and you liked it, but your bosses didn't.

176
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:41,920
Then that way, you're the good guy,

177
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:43,280
and they're the bad guy.

178
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:45,810
That's good. I liked it, they didn't.

179
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:50,870
Joey, for God's sake, go to work.

180
00:07:55,990 --> 00:07:59,180
I can't believe I'm about to meet Benjamin Hobart.

181
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:01,300
I've always thought of him as someone I'd invite...

182
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:04,080
...to my fantasy dinner party.

183
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:06,290
Do you think there's any chance

184
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:08,690
he'll bring Christie Brinkley or C-3PO?

185
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:12,740
Sorry, it looks like it's just him.

186
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:16,040
Charlie.

187
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:22,580
My God, you look absolutely stunning.

188
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:25,600
Well, I am having a good hair day.

189
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:29,840
- It's so good to see you. - Oh, you too.

190
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,120
I'm okay.

191
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:39,390
I'm sorry. Ross Geller, Benjamin Hobart.

192
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,130
It's an honor to meet you.

193
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:43,280
I can't tell you how long...

194
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:47,580
...I've been an admirer of your work. I mean, that Nobel Prize.

195
00:08:49,430 --> 00:08:51,200
I mean, I have to tell you

196
00:08:51,250 --> 00:08:53,940
that you're one of the reasons I got into the field.

197
00:08:54,290 --> 00:08:55,970
Well, likewise.

198
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,380
Actually not likewise.

199
00:08:58,430 --> 00:09:00,130
I'd never heard of you until this morning.

200
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,900
But it's nice to be nice.

201
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:06,620
- Shall we? - Yeah. Thank you.

202
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:13,200
I can't believe that you chose this restaurant.

203
00:09:13,790 --> 00:09:15,030
Do you remember the night?

204
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:17,640
Oh, my God. I completely forgot.

205
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:22,690
Oh, my God, I can't believe they let us back in this place.

206
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:31,820
You weren't there.

207
00:09:33,310 --> 00:09:36,620
No, but, you know, it's just a funny image.

208
00:09:36,670 --> 00:09:41,300
You know, the two of you in this restaurant with the....

209
00:09:43,690 --> 00:09:45,880
Ross, why don't you tell Benji

210
00:09:45,930 --> 00:09:48,190
about your proposal while I go to the ladies' room.

211
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:52,530
So tell me about it.

212
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:56,830
Okay. Well, I would like to do a dig in the Painted Desert.

213
00:09:56,880 --> 00:10:00,540
There are still several areas that haven't been fully excavated.

214
00:10:00,590 --> 00:10:01,900
- Break up with Charlie. - What?

215
00:10:01,950 --> 00:10:02,670
What?

216
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:08,760
Did you just say, "Break up with Charlie"?

217
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:11,410
Well, yes and no.

218
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:14,390
Yes, I did say it. And no, I didn't not say it.

219
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:18,220
Kind of inappropriate, don't you think?

220
00:10:18,270 --> 00:10:20,190
Listen, I'm sorry.

221
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,610
I just haven't seen her for so long,

222
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,730
all these feelings are rushing back.

223
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:24,750
I'm starting to realize

224
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,420
how much I've missed her.

225
00:10:26,470 --> 00:10:28,780
And I'm gonna need you to break up with her.

226
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,470
Are you serious?

227
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,910
If you say, yes, then I'm serious.

228
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:35,770
If you say, no, then I'm joking.

229
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:39,320
- No. - Joking it is.

230
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:45,080
Hi, sorry I'm late.

231
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:46,540
Hey, how'd it go with Mike?

232
00:10:46,590 --> 00:10:47,960
Is he gonna let you keep the painting?

233
00:10:48,010 --> 00:10:50,350
No, he really hates it.

234
00:10:50,610 --> 00:10:53,420
But he's gonna let me keep my box of human hair.

235
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,800
So you gotta pick your battles.

236
00:10:57,310 --> 00:11:00,210
But the good news is, Gladys is yours.

237
00:11:02,010 --> 00:11:03,750
Wow, what's the bad news?

238
00:11:04,930 --> 00:11:06,070
Who's Gladys?

239
00:11:06,190 --> 00:11:08,280
Oh, she's that work of art I made.

240
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:10,560
You know, with the woman coming out of the frame.

241
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:14,870
And Monica gets to keep her?

242
00:11:15,850 --> 00:11:19,160
In her house? I am so jealous.

243
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:23,130
I didn't know you wanted her too.

244
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:28,010
Well, I mean, sure, of course.

245
00:11:29,090 --> 00:11:31,390
But you already gave that to Monica, so....

246
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:33,560
You know, I would give her up for you.

247
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:35,110
No, I couldn't let you do that.

248
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:37,690
- No, but I want to. - But I don't want you to.

249
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:41,830
- But I insist. - But I insist harder.

250
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:46,100
Girls. Girls. Stop. Okay, we'll flip a coin.

251
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:47,110
Heads, she's Rachel's.

252
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:48,450
Tails, she's Monica's.

253
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:53,560
Tails. Monica, she's yours.

254
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:55,560
No, that landed in your food.

255
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:57,730
No, no, that's okay.

256
00:11:57,780 --> 00:12:00,170
You won fair and square. I'm so sad.

257
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,140
Hey, Joe?

258
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:06,870
- What's up? - Bad news.

259
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:07,730
I watched the tape

260
00:12:07,730 --> 00:12:09,090
and passed it along to my bosses

261
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:10,820
and they weren't interested.

262
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:14,140
I'm sorry, man.

263
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:18,530
But you watched the tape?

264
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:20,850
Yeah, I liked it.

265
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,560
But my bosses didn't go for it.

266
00:12:24,610 --> 00:12:26,770
Stupid sons of bitches.

267
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:33,620
You didn't watch the tape.

268
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:36,420
What? Of course I did.

269
00:12:36,470 --> 00:12:38,570
Look, it's one thing not to cast me,

270
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,550
but to lie to me?

271
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,690
I'm not lying to you. I watched it.

272
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:43,080
You lied again.

273
00:12:43,130 --> 00:12:46,080
- I watched it. - Keep going, Pinocchio.

274
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,450
- I did. - No, you didn't.

275
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:51,630
I'm telling you, I watched the tape.

276
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,550
- Did you watch the tape? - No.

277
00:12:59,690 --> 00:13:01,280
All right. The selection committee has chosen

278
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,230
the three of you as our finalists.

279
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,120
The ultimate decision will be based on the answers

280
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,170
you give to the questions I ask.

281
00:13:07,170 --> 00:13:08,860
We're gonna go ahead and start with Dr. Li.

282
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:11,050
Dr. Li, you claim the field is too reliant

283
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:13,340
on the Linnaean taxonomic system.

284
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,470
How do you propose to correct this problem?

285
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:16,870
Well, I believe that the answers

286
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:18,740
lie in the osteological evidence.

287
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:20,790
- I plan to begin there. - Interesting.

288
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:22,290
I guess.

289
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:26,420
Dr. Biely, your proposal includes some fieldwork.

290
00:13:26,470 --> 00:13:27,700
Where might that take place?

291
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:30,580
Primarily in the Pierre Shale region of South Dakota.

292
00:13:30,630 --> 00:13:32,500
Certainly. Very well.

293
00:13:32,550 --> 00:13:35,270
And Dr.Geller, when is my birthday?

294
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:42,870
What? I--

295
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:46,990
Care to venture a guess?

296
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:53,910
- May 12? - That's not even kind of close.

297
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:57,510
Dr. Li, how many graduate students you'd be needing?

298
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,400
Half a dozen.

299
00:13:58,450 --> 00:13:59,750
I see. And Dr. Biely?

300
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,200
Three for excavation, and two for analysis.

301
00:14:02,250 --> 00:14:06,480
Certainly. Dr. Geller, which 1965 Shirelles hit...

302
00:14:06,530 --> 00:14:09,250
...was later covered by a popular British Invasion band?

303
00:14:13,110 --> 00:14:15,960
What? I need six graduate students.

304
00:14:16,010 --> 00:14:17,040
No, I'm sorry.

305
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:18,890
We were looking for "Baby It's You."

306
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,320
"Baby It's You."

307
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,220
What? Wait just a minute.

308
00:14:25,270 --> 00:14:28,540
None of my questions have anything to do with paleontology.

309
00:14:28,590 --> 00:14:29,580
You're right, I apologize.

310
00:14:29,630 --> 00:14:31,020
Scratch the last question.

311
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:33,300
Spell "Boscodictiasaur."

312
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:39,210
I've never heard of a "Boscodictiasaur."

313
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:41,270
Yeah, I just made it up. Spell it.

314
00:14:44,530 --> 00:14:46,580
Okay. B-O-S-

315
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,010
No, it starts with a silent M.

316
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:49,650
Oh, come on!

317
00:14:57,350 --> 00:14:59,150
I can't believe Joey.

318
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,970
I hate being called a liar.

319
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,860
But you are a liar.

320
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,430
What did I just say?

321
00:15:07,310 --> 00:15:08,270
Are you still here?

322
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,410
Yes. And I have to say.

323
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:11,860
And I'm not just hurt, I'm insulted.

324
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:13,670
When I tell somebody I did something--

325
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,480
Okay, hold on, let me just stop you right there, okay?

326
00:15:15,530 --> 00:15:17,550
First, you lied. Right?

327
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,360
Then you lied about lying, okay?

328
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:22,100
Then you lied about

329
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:23,580
lying about lying, okay?

330
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:25,030
So before you lie about

331
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:28,470
lying about lying about lying about lying....

332
00:15:30,790 --> 00:15:32,210
Stop lying.

333
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,140
Why are you so sure

334
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:35,500
I didn't watch this tape?

335
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:36,420
You wanna know why?

336
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:37,510
You wanna know why?

337
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:39,750
Well, this is going well.

338
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,580
Here's how I know you didn't watch.

339
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:45,530
If you had seen what was on this tape,

340
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:48,600
believe me, you'd have some comments.

341
00:15:48,650 --> 00:15:51,590
All right, remember, I got paid a lot of money for this...

342
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:53,470
...and it only aired in Japan.

343
00:15:54,710 --> 00:15:56,090
Ichiban.

344
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,000
Ichiban, lipstick for men.

345
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,600
Ichiban, lipstick for men.

346
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:21,770
And that's how I know you didn't watch the tape.

347
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,900
He really is a chameleon.

348
00:16:34,150 --> 00:16:38,010
Well, Gladys, say hello to your new home.

349
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:44,400
- Oh, my. - Wow.

350
00:16:44,450 --> 00:16:47,740
Oh, she is so nice and big.

351
00:16:49,610 --> 00:16:54,210
Oh, Monica, where are you going to display Gladys,

352
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:55,940
oh, so proudly?

353
00:16:56,790 --> 00:16:58,910
I haven't really settled on a spot yet.

354
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:01,150
How about right above the TV?

355
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:04,060
That way, it will be the first thing that you see

356
00:17:04,110 --> 00:17:05,620
when you walk in the door.

357
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,350
Yeah, yeah,

358
00:17:08,490 --> 00:17:10,290
and you can get rid of that French poster.

359
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:12,630
- I like that poster. - Really?

360
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:14,980
It doesn't have anything coming out of it.

361
00:17:16,170 --> 00:17:18,680
Or maybe there's someplace for her in your bedroom?

362
00:17:18,730 --> 00:17:20,190
There's nothing above your bed.

363
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:21,520
Are you still here?

364
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:27,230
Oh, hi. Hello.

365
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:32,270
Have you come to ask me some more paleontology-related questions?

366
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,930
Your grandmother's nickname, perhaps?

367
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:36,880
Aunt Margaret's pants size?

368
00:17:39,130 --> 00:17:41,220
I've come here to apologize.

369
00:17:41,270 --> 00:17:43,840
I think I may have let my feelings...

370
00:17:43,890 --> 00:17:46,760
...for Charlie interfere with the interview process.

371
00:17:46,810 --> 00:17:48,580
No. Stop.

372
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:52,350
Anyway, I decided to offer you the grant.

373
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:54,960
Really?

374
00:17:55,010 --> 00:17:58,860
There is just one small stipulation.

375
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:00,670
I have to break up with Charlie?

376
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,600
Hey, you got one right.

377
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,850
You're crazy.

378
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,500
Crazy or romantic?

379
00:18:09,490 --> 00:18:10,630
Crazy.

380
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:15,240
- Or? - Get out!

381
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:23,170
Oh, my God.

382
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:25,890
What?

383
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:29,670
Joey, what is this thing doing here?

384
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,040
I got her from Monica.

385
00:18:31,090 --> 00:18:33,710
She sold it to me for a very reasonable price.

386
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,420
Joey, we're not keeping this.

387
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:38,180
But it's an original Buffay.

388
00:18:41,570 --> 00:18:44,030
All right, fine. You can keep it.

389
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:46,470
As long as you don't mind that she's haunted.

390
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:48,310
Hey, what? What?

391
00:18:48,850 --> 00:18:51,010
Well, legend has it, Joey,

392
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:53,500
that she comes alive when you're asleep.

393
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:58,790
She climbs out of the frame...

394
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:01,600
...and then drags her half-a-body

395
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:03,200
across the floor...

396
00:19:03,250 --> 00:19:05,300
...just looking for legs to steal.

397
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:09,080
And then with her one good hand...

398
00:19:09,130 --> 00:19:13,140
...she slowly reaches up...

399
00:19:13,190 --> 00:19:15,450
...and turns your doorknob.

400
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:18,880
Get that legless witch out of here!

401
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:26,810
Hey, I sold that to Joey.

402
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:28,320
Yeah, well, I told him it's haunted.

403
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:29,530
Two can play at this game.

404
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:31,160
Too late. You can't give it back.

405
00:19:31,210 --> 00:19:31,940
Oh, yes, I can.

406
00:19:31,990 --> 00:19:33,580
No, you can't, she's yours.

407
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:35,160
- She's yours. - She's yours.

408
00:19:35,210 --> 00:19:36,480
She's yours.

409
00:19:36,530 --> 00:19:37,420
Hey.

410
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:40,790
- She's mine. - She's mine.

411
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,650
- She's mine. - She's mine.

412
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:45,370
You guys, you don't have to fight over her anymore.

413
00:19:46,530 --> 00:19:47,930
Whoever doesn't get Gladys,

414
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:49,410
gets Glynnis.

415
00:19:57,890 --> 00:19:59,590
- I want Gladys. - She's mine.

416
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:02,560
- She's mine. - She's mine.

417
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:08,470
I know. Look, I'm sorry I didn't give them your tape.

418
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:10,520
And I promise next time to submit you,

419
00:20:10,570 --> 00:20:12,570
whether I think you're right or not.

420
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:14,270
That's not the point, Chandler.

421
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,840
The point is that you lied.

422
00:20:15,890 --> 00:20:17,810
I know. You're right.

423
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,220
What's it gonna take for you to forgive me?

424
00:20:20,540 --> 00:20:22,070
Oh, my God.

425
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,360
Excellent.

426
00:20:28,890 --> 00:20:30,450
Now what do you say?

427
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:33,360
Lying is wrong.

428
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,250
And? And?

429
00:20:38,110 --> 00:20:39,930
I'm a pretty little girl.

430
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:43,850
I knew it.

431
00:20:51,730 --> 00:20:54,250
Your ex-boyfriend is insane.

432
00:20:55,510 --> 00:20:56,470
Did you get the grant?

433
00:20:56,470 --> 00:20:58,270
No. And you wanna know why?

434
00:20:58,270 --> 00:21:01,670
Because your ex-boyfriend is still in love with you.

435
00:21:01,890 --> 00:21:02,830
- What? - Yeah.

436
00:21:02,830 --> 00:21:03,600
He wouldn't give me the grant,

437
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,460
because I wouldn't give you up.

438
00:21:05,510 --> 00:21:07,190
Benji isn't in love with me.

439
00:21:07,190 --> 00:21:08,990
I mean, he broke up with me.

440
00:21:08,990 --> 00:21:11,260
And besides, he's a very ethical man.

441
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:12,830
Really?

442
00:21:14,130 --> 00:21:17,170
Is it ethical to ask someone in a grant review:

443
00:21:17,220 --> 00:21:19,110
"Who was the voice of Underdog?"

444
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:21,490
I'm sure he was just joking, Ross.

445
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,570
If you don't believe me, let's go talk to him.

446
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:24,340
I'm telling you,

447
00:21:24,390 --> 00:21:27,120
he didn't ask me one paleontological question.

448
00:21:27,170 --> 00:21:27,960
Seriously?

449
00:21:28,010 --> 00:21:30,220
Oh, I'm sorry. No, he did ask me one:

450
00:21:30,270 --> 00:21:32,710
"How do you spell Boscodictiasaur?"

451
00:21:32,760 --> 00:21:35,030
Well, if it's like the Lake Mbosco in Congo,

452
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,160
then M-B-O--

453
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:37,190
Damn it.

454
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:44,540
Dr. Geller. Charlie, what are you doing here?

455
00:21:44,590 --> 00:21:46,700
I want you to tell her everything.

456
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:48,580
About the deal you tried to make with me,

457
00:21:48,630 --> 00:21:50,780
about the crazy questions you--

458
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:55,260
Wally Cox. That's the voice of Underdog.

459
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:58,800
Like I tried to tell you in the interview...

460
00:21:58,850 --> 00:22:00,530
...this grant is not based on

461
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:02,930
your knowledge of pretty useless trivia.

462
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,580
No, don't do that.

463
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:06,510
I want you to look her in the eyes

464
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,890
and tell her the truth.

465
00:22:09,390 --> 00:22:10,340
Benji?

466
00:22:11,590 --> 00:22:13,000
All right. It's true.

467
00:22:13,050 --> 00:22:14,280
I behaved horribly,

468
00:22:14,330 --> 00:22:16,450
but it's only because I still love you.

469
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:17,930
And I would do anything

470
00:22:17,980 --> 00:22:19,380
to have you back in my life.

471
00:22:19,450 --> 00:22:21,400
Too little, too late, Benji.

472
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:25,290
I can't believe this.

473
00:22:25,340 --> 00:22:27,580
I never should've broken up with you.

474
00:22:27,630 --> 00:22:29,870
I think about you all the time.

475
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:32,850
Do you ever still think about me?

476
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:34,070
No.

477
00:22:35,290 --> 00:22:36,800
- Yes. - What?

478
00:22:38,330 --> 00:22:40,380
I don't know what to say, Benji.

479
00:22:40,430 --> 00:22:41,800
This is all so...

480
00:22:42,390 --> 00:22:44,000
...romantic.

481
00:22:45,180 --> 00:22:46,650
Or?

482
00:22:49,230 --> 00:22:51,700
I know I may be way out of bounds here...

483
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:54,680
...but is there any chance you would take me back?

484
00:22:57,790 --> 00:22:59,030
Maybe.

485
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,750
Sweetie, this conversation is starting to

486
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,690
make me a little uncomfortable.

487
00:23:05,710 --> 00:23:09,440
Oh, God. I am so sorry, but--

488
00:23:09,490 --> 00:23:13,900
I mean, there's so much history between us, you know?

489
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:16,050
I'm sorry too.

490
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:26,230
I love you.

491
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:28,110
I love you too.

492
00:23:30,860 --> 00:23:33,840
Okay, that's it, we are seeing other people.

493
00:23:54,180 --> 00:23:55,610
Gladys?

494
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:03,840
For the third time this week.

495
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:06,180
Man, this does not get old.

496
00:24:07,250 --> 00:24:08,100
You're mean!

497
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:11,280
Oh, don't be such a baby. Please.

